# Paths a PAST release installed and a LATER release deleted.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. tools/updater._prunable normally admits a path only
# when the install's OLD MANIFEST.sha256 lists it -- condition (c), the safety
# property that stops the prune pass deleting a tester's own file. That
# condition cannot reach a file STRANDED by a release that predates the prune:
# it was installed by an older release whose manifest listed it, and that
# manifest has since been overwritten, so no evidence of it survives on the
# client. This file is that evidence, shipped forward -- the release states
# plainly what it expects gone.
#
# It REPLACES condition (c) with a different safety property: an explicit,
# human-authored, code-reviewed list inside a SIGNED release, rather than an
# inference from client state. Every other guard still applies to every entry
# below -- a listed path is deleted only when it is absent from the new release
# tree, is not protected/derived/never-prune, and the release tree carried its
# own MANIFEST.sha256. Each deletion is backed up before unlink and restored if
# the swap fails.
#
# THE RITUAL: a dead-code batch that deletes a SHIPPED module adds its dist
# path here in the SAME commit. Forgetting re-creates exactly the bug this
# closes -- see operations/runbook.md -> "Files a release removes".
#
# FORMAT: one install-relative POSIX path per line. Blank lines and #-comments
# are ignored. Absolute paths, drive letters, backslashes and any `..`
# component are DROPPED with a warning, never honoured.

# --- 2026-08-30: stranded on every install built before the prune pass -------
# Measured on the live 1.60.4 install. None appear in the 1.60.4 manifest, so
# the forward-looking pass can never see them. Several were deleted so the
# capability could not be revived (docs/RETIRED_CAPABILITIES.md).
tools/comment_reconciler.py
tools/image_description.py
tools/jira_attachments.py
